// What an argument letter of a builtin's signature (conf.id's bkk_bi_sig,
// or the letters bkg_usig writes for a function of the program) means. i f
// s I F S are exact types; l is any list, a a string or any list, and e the
// element type of the first argument. bkg_fits says whether a type
// satisfies a letter, bkg_wantof the exact type a letter asks for (a hint
// for list literals, 0 when it asks for none), bkg_retty the type of a result
// letter, and bkg_letname how an error message names what a letter wanted.

